From: SurNet <surnet@localhost>
Date: Mon, 18 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93: enable on EcoNet EN7528/EN751221

The EcoNet EN7528 (and EN751221) SoCs integrate an Inside Secure
SafeXcel EIP-93 crypto engine at a fixed MMIO window (0x1fb70000 on
EN7528, GIC shared interrupt source 28), identified from the stock
EN7561D crypto_k.ko and vendor GIC source table
(PCI id 0x16ae:0x0093, HWPAL device "SafeXcel_EIP_93").

Two changes are needed versus the MT7621 integration:
 - allow the driver to build on ECONET;
 - unlike MT7621 (where the block is permanently clocked and out of
   reset), here the crypto clock is a fixed-rate always-on clock but the
   block is left held in reset by the bootloader, so probe must deassert
   the reset (and enable the optional clock) before touching any
   register. Both are optional so existing MT7621 platforms are
   unaffected. An early identification read is logged to confirm the
   engine responds at the configured base.

Signed-off-by: SurNet <surnet@localhost>
---
--- a/drivers/crypto/inside-secure/eip93/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/crypto/inside-secure/eip93/Kconfig
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
 config CRYPTO_DEV_EIP93
 	tristate "Support for EIP93 crypto HW accelerators"
-	depends on SOC_MT7621 || ARCH_AIROHA ||COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on SOC_MT7621 || ARCH_AIROHA || ECONET || COMPILE_TEST
 	select CRYPTO_LIB_AES
 	select CRYPTO_LIB_DES
 	select CRYPTO_SKCIPHER
--- a/drivers/crypto/inside-secure/eip93/eip93-main.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/inside-secure/eip93/eip93-main.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/reset.h>
 #include <linux/spinlock.h>
 #include <crypto/aes.h>
 #include <crypto/ctr.h>
@@ -412,6 +413,8 @@
 {
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
 	struct eip93_device *eip93;
+	struct reset_control *rstc;
+	struct clk *clk;
 	u32 ver, algo_flags;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -426,6 +429,36 @@
 	if (IS_ERR(eip93->base))
 		return PTR_ERR(eip93->base);
 
+	/*
+	 * EcoNet EN7528/EN751221: bring the crypto block out of gate/reset
+	 * before touching any register. Unlike the MT7621 integration (where
+	 * the block is always clocked), here the crypto clock/reset are
+	 * software-controlled and the bootloader leaves the engine held in
+	 * reset -- reading registers first would otherwise return reset-state
+	 * garbage (or on a gated bus, hang). Both are optional so other SoCs
+	 * that lack them keep working unchanged.
+	 */
+	clk = devm_clk_get_optional_enabled(dev, NULL);
+	if (IS_ERR(clk))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(clk),
+				     "failed to enable crypto clock\n");
+
+	rstc = devm_reset_control_get_optional_exclusive(dev, NULL);
+	if (IS_ERR(rstc))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(rstc),
+				     "failed to get crypto reset\n");
+	reset_control_deassert(rstc);
+	usleep_range(10, 20);
+
+	/*
+	 * Early identification read. Confirms the engine actually responds at
+	 * this base address before the rest of probe programs the rings.
+	 */
+	ver = readl(eip93->base + EIP93_REG_PE_REVISION);
+	dev_info(dev, "EIP93 id: REV=0x%08x OPT0=0x%08x OPT1=0x%08x\n",
+		 ver, readl(eip93->base + EIP93_REG_PE_OPTION_0),
+		 readl(eip93->base + EIP93_REG_PE_OPTION_1));
+
 	eip93->irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 0);
 	if (eip93->irq < 0)
 		return eip93->irq;
